    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "巳十二月屆（一ニ田村春馬　福井ナシ）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "巳十二月届（一に田村春馬　福井なし）（みどし じゅうにがつ とどけ・いつに たむら はるま・ふくい なし）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Small-type note under Fukui Daizō's name, set as three short runs. In the return of the 12th month of the snake year (Meiji 2/12, early 1870) this post is given as Tamura Haruma, and Fukui does not appear at all. The date tag stands in the rightmost run and is therefore read first; the parenthesis opens at the head of the middle run and closes at the foot of the leftmost. It is the second of the two amendments on this leaf drawn from the same 12th-month return, the other being the bracketed insert in the upper register about Toda Tetsuya."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "福井大造割註"
      }
